<title>MEXICO: Serfin to report 1996 results on Tuesday.</title>
<headline>Serfin to report 1996 results on Tuesday.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Grupo Financiero Serfin, owner of Banca Serfin, will report 1996 earnings to the Bolsa on Tuesday, spokesman Roberto Aguirre told Reuters.</p>
<p>He was unable to say whether an alliance with HSBC Holdings Plc would be announced at the same time. Negotiations have been underway for months to sell a 19.9 percent stake of Serfin to the London-based bank.</p>
<p>Serfin, Mexico's third largest banking group, is expected to report a large 1996 loss as it aggressively writes off past-due loans to prepare itself for the sale, analysts said.</p>
<p>((--Henry Tricks, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9560))</p>
